---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
---
<Shell title="About Langston" section="about">
  <div class="about-page">
    <header class="page-heading about-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE PLAYBOOK</p>
      <h1>Hi, I’m Langston.</h1>
      <p class="lede">I’m learning, building, and figuring out better ways to make technology easier to understand.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-story">
      <p>I work in IT support and I’m currently studying artificial intelligence at Kennesaw State University. I earned my B.S. in Computer Information Systems with a minor in Cybersecurity from Western Carolina University in 2026.</p>

      <p>A lot of what I’ve learned about technology has come from actually using it, breaking things, fixing them, and trying to understand why something works the way it does.</p>

      <p>I also ran track in college. It may seem unrelated, but that experience taught me a lot about consistency, patience, and improving a little at a time — which is pretty similar to how I approach learning technology.</p>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Why I made this</h2>
        <p>When I started using AI tools to build and improve websites, I noticed how easy it was to get stuck on one simple problem: knowing what to ask.</p>

        <p>You might know that something looks wrong, feels confusing, or needs to work better without knowing the technical name for it. That shouldn’t stop you from improving it.</p>

        <p>That’s why I made UI Prompt Package — to give beginners a clearer starting point.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>What I want this to be</h2>
        <p>This isn’t meant to be a giant library of complicated prompts. I want it to feel more like a practical playbook you can come back to whenever you’re stuck.</p>

        <p>Each prompt should help you understand what you’re changing, why it matters, and how to make it fit your own project.</p>

        <p>I’m still learning too. I’ll keep improving the playbook as I learn what works, what doesn’t, and what would make things easier for someone starting from scratch.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="about-cta" aria-labelledby="about-cta-title">
      <div>
        <p class="tiny">START SMALL</p>
        <h2 id="about-cta-title">Ready to try one?</h2>
        <p>Start with a beginner-friendly prompt and customize it for your own project.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button primary" href="/start">Try your first prompt</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Shell>